# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend build-time configuration
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the bundle at build time. Do not put
# secrets here — anything in this file ends up in the shipped JavaScript.
#
# On Vercel, set these in Project → Settings → Environment Variables, not here.
# A `.env` file is not deployed, and Vercel needs its own copy of the values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL for API calls.
#
# Leave unset for a same-origin deployment (Option A — the Laravel container
# serves both the SPA and /api), which is what the Docker and Render paths use.
# `src/api/client.js` then falls back to the relative `/api`.
#
# Set it to the absolute backend URL when the SPA is deployed separately
# (Option B), which is the Vercel + Render split. The trailing /api is
# required — the client appends `/auth/login` and so on to this value.
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://YOUR-APP.onrender.com/api
#
# Getting this wrong produces a blank page or a network error on every call:
# the bundle has the URL baked in at build time, so changing it requires a
# redeploy on Vercel, not just a settings change.
# VITE_API_URL=

# Dev-only: where `npm run dev` proxies /api requests. Ignored in production
# builds because the proxy only exists on the Vite dev server.
VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8000

# Public site name shown in the browser title and the public leaderboard shell.
VITE_APP_NAME=PSM Management System
